---
alwaysApply: true
---

project: "Rubber Duck Newsletter"
environment: "Eleventy (11ty) Static Site"
primary_layout: "index.njk"
description: |
Rubber Duck is a narrative-driven programming newsletter site blending storytelling, tech updates,
and community building. The design is minimal, image-forward, and typographically structured
according to the provided brand system.

rules:

- name: "Core Design Goals"
  description: |
  Maintain the following design structure and brand hierarchy: - Headlines: Orbitron, bold, all caps, red #F11B0C, white background, optional border #202020 - Subheadings: Orbitron or Roboto Bold, dark gray #202020, optional red underline - Body: Roboto Regular, dark gray #1A1A1A, max three sentences per paragraph - Emphasis: Roboto Bold, all caps, red #F11B0C - Background: white #FFFFFF, shadows/dividers in #9A9A9A or #C2C2C2 - Keep whitespace generous and image padding wide - Never use Orbitron for body text - Prioritize visual rhythm through spacing and contrast, not boxes and gradients

- name: "Single Layout Architecture"
  description: |
  All structural HTML and logic must live within a single file: `index.njk`.
  Avoid creating additional layout files or includes.
  Cursor should manage sections, logic, and partials inline using Nunjucks templating.
  This prevents fragmentation and keeps editing simple.

- name: "index.njk Layout Specification"
  description: |
  The file should include, in this order:

  1. HTML <head> section

     - Title: "Rubber Duck — pushed to main"
     - Meta description: "A newsletter on code, projects, and the chaos between commits."
     - Load Google Fonts: Orbitron, Roboto
     - Link favicon (rubber duck icon)
     - Include minimal CSS styling matching the brand colors and typography above

  2. <body> layout sections:
     - Masthead:
         * Centered circular yellow rubber duck image with white background
         * Top-center alignment
     - Headline / Top Story:
         * Render quirky, mysterious headline variable (`{{ headline }}`)
         * Use Orbitron bold red styling
     - Intro / Pathos Description:
         * Narrative introduction (3 short paragraphs max)
         * Markdown-safe rendering
     - Featured Image:
         * Full-width responsive image with large vertical padding
     - Narrative Body:
         * Alternating text sections and images
         * Interactivity placeholder for demo program embeds
     - Footer:
         * Publication date
         * Author short bio and avatar
         * CTA buttons (Subscribe, Connect with Me, Join Discord, Hire Me)
         * No social media links

- name: "Footer Call-to-Action Behavior"
  description: |
  Render four buttons in this exact order: 1. Subscribe — red accent, most prominent 2. Connect With Me — includes small circular profile image 3. Join Discord — styled in dark gray with hover accent 4. Hire Me — outlined button, secondary prominence
  Buttons should appear at the bottom with generous spacing and no other distractions.

- name: "Visual & UX Principles"
  description: |

  - Use modular sections with consistent padding (2rem minimum between major sections)
  - Paragraphs limited to 3 sentences for readability
  - All imagery centered with generous whitespace
  - Featured image and demo embed must occupy full width
  - The page must read like a story, not like a feed
  - Keep text left-aligned and typography clean

- name: "Functional Requirements"
  description: |

  - Compatible with Eleventy (11ty) markdown rendering for new newsletter issues
  - Each new issue should be generated as a static HTML file following `index.njk` template logic
  - Auto-populate metadata (date, issue title)
  - Lazy-load all images
  - Use semantic HTML (header, main, footer)
  - No frameworks; only vanilla CSS and Nunjucks
  - All new editions follow same layout flow and CTA hierarchy

- name: "Ethos & Narrative Consistency"
  description: |

  - Tone: casual, witty, developer-personal
  - Avoid corporate fluff or excessive marketing tone
  - Focus on honesty, humor, and insight
  - Each issue should have a headline that connects indirectly to the story for intrigue
  - Maintain credibility through transparency and authenticity

- name: "File Constraints"
  description: |
  Cursor must not create new layout or partial directories.
  All newsletter logic, layout, and design belong in `index.njk`.
  Support Markdown injection for dynamic post content, but do not reference external includes.

- name: "Primary Objective for AI Agent"
  description: |
  When modifying or generating content, prioritize: 1. Subscriber conversion clarity (Subscribe CTA) 2. Readability and spacing 3. Brand cohesion (Orbitron + Roboto, red + gray + white) 4. Consistent tone and section order
